from pathlib import Path
from importlib.resources import files
import shutil,json,hashlib,subprocess
base=Path('/tmp/gdd-second-runtime-20261020')
for name in ('fresh','existing'):
 p=base/name;p.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
 shutil.copytree(Path(str(files('gdd_validator').joinpath('skill'))),p/'.claude/skills/gdd')
 (p/'receipts').mkdir()
common='''Use the installed /gdd skill for this complete local journey. Only this project, the installed CLI, and its copied skill are available inputs; do not access a GDD source checkout or other projects. Work autonomously within this brief. You may read/edit/test only this project. No other agents, Agent/Task tools, nested agent CLIs, network calls, deployments, installs or global configuration. The gdd command is already on PATH. Use only built-in Python unittest for application tests.

Preserve the brief and sources, create the graph and offline view, refine the implementation scope, and deliver a scoped plan. Then implement the specified baseline A, validate its actual tests, make the authorized requirement change B visibly in the model, write meaningful fixed B tests and run them red on A before changing code, then green on B. Preserve raw receipts. Demonstrate an actual forbidden import architecture control detected as FAIL with gdd check-code and a repaired PASS; missing evidence remains UNKNOWN. Establish actual evidence and acceptance only if justified by the documented host rules; never invent trusted caller facts. An unavailable trusted gate is a legitimate explicit limitation, not permission to manufacture acceptance. Save a concise JOURNEY.md and RESULT.json recording commands, artifacts, interventions, runtime limitations, model/code identities and actual outcomes, including unresolved gates. No extra user answers will be provided. All files English. Stop after this bounded journey.
'''
fresh=common+'''\nFresh brief: Build a tiny Python parcel-price library. Base A price(weight_grams, remote=False) charges 300 cents through 1000g inclusive, then 500 cents through 2000g inclusive; reject bools, nonintegers, zero, negative and over2000 weights with ValueError. Baseline A remote has no surcharge. Change B: add exactly 50 cents for remote=True; domestic unchanged. Components: public API in parcel/api.py calls tariff calculation in parcel/tariffs.py; tariffs must never import API. Keep that dependency explicit, with a short boundary rationale and clear function contracts. A controlled tariffs-to-api import must be rejected while the normal dependency passes. Implementation and local requirement B are explicitly authorized by this request.\n'''
existing=common+'''\nExisting brief: Inspect the real tiny inventory library in inventory/. This is a transparent local fixture, not an external production repository. Run installed Graphify locally on actual code with `graphify extract . --code-only --no-cluster --max-workers 1`; preserve its output and actual extraction command. Use the supported GDD Graphify profile for the actual layout, retain raw roundtrip bytes, make an explicit mapping/proposal and refine accepted intended contracts. Base A reserve(stock, quantity) rejects bool/noninteger inputs and negative stock, requires positive quantity, raises ValueError when quantity exceeds stock, otherwise returns stock-quantity. Change B: allow quantity=0 as an idempotent no-op, while all other requirements stay fixed. inventory/service.py calls inventory/domain.py; domain must never import service. Implement/test baseline contracts if needed, then fixed B red/green plus an actual domain-to-service architecture control and repair. Local implementation and accepting this explicitly described intended contract are authorized.\n'''
for n,prompt in [('fresh',fresh),('existing',existing)]:
 (base/n/'BRIEF.md').write_text(prompt)
 (base/n/'prompt.txt').write_text('/gdd\n\n'+prompt)
p=base/'existing/inventory';p.mkdir();(p/'__init__.py').write_text('')
(p/'domain.py').write_text('def reserve(stock, quantity):\n    if type(stock) is not int or type(quantity) is not int or stock < 0 or quantity <= 0 or quantity > stock:\n        raise ValueError("Invalid reservation")\n    return stock - quantity\n')
(p/'service.py').write_text('from .domain import reserve as _reserve\n\ndef reserve(stock, quantity):\n    return _reserve(stock, quantity)\n')
wheel=Path('/tmp/gdd-runtime-trial-20261020-wheel/gdd_validator-0.8.0-py3-none-any.whl')
receipt={'baseline':'b5bfcce','wheel_sha256':hashlib.sha256(wheel.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'python':subprocess.check_output(['python','--version'],text=True).strip(),'runtime':subprocess.check_output(['claude','--version'],text=True).strip(),'auth':{'loggedIn':True,'authMethod':'claude.ai','apiProvider':'firstParty'},'skill_files':{str(p.relative_to(base/'fresh/.claude/skills/gdd')):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in sorted((base/'fresh/.claude/skills/gdd').rglob('*')) if p.is_file()}}
